    <!--
        opentelemetry-semconv (transitive)
        No fix released yet; expected with the next Quarkus release.

        opentelemetry-semconv is a pure constants/attribute-name library without runtime
        logic. Additionally, the project does not declare quarkus-opentelemetry, so no
        OTel exporter or instrumentation pipeline is active.
    -->
    <suppress until="2026-08-31Z">
        <!-- started: 2026-05-04 | affected: NO (constants-only lib, OTel not enabled) -->
        <cve>CVE-2026-39883</cve>
    </suppress>

    <!--
        netty-transport (transitive) - CPE false positive.

        CVE-2026-56816 is an HTTP/3 DoS (CWE-400): an attacker sends HTTP/3 reserved frames
        with large unvalidated payload lengths across many streams, causing memory exhaustion.
        The advisory (GHSA-hpcc-26xq-25fv) lists a single affected artifact,
        io.netty:netty-codec-http3 (< 4.2.16.Final), a 4.2.x/incubator-only module. It does
        not reference netty-transport at all; the match here comes from the generic
        cpe:2.3:a:netty:netty CPE.

        netty-codec-http3 is not on the classpath (not in the dependency tree) and the app
        uses no HTTP/3, so the vulnerable code path does not exist.
        RE-EVALUATE if netty-codec-http3 / HTTP/3 is ever pulled in.
    -->
    <suppress until="2026-08-31Z">
        <!-- started: 2026-08-03 | affected: NO (CPE false positive; vuln is in netty-codec-http3, not used) -->
        <cve>CVE-2026-56816</cve>
    </suppress>
</suppressions>
